  "reputation": {
    "summary": "Nisshinbo says it carries the MUSES01/02 sound concept, with layout and lead frame tuned for mass production. Japanese reviewers hear MUSES02-like sound with thinner lines, deep bass and softened top treble. Head-Fi posters call it the 'least opamp-sounding', tube-like and wide-staged. Rankings place it above NJM4580/NJM8801, below newer or JFET parts.",
    "sonic_descriptors": [
      "deep, full bass",
      "wide soundstage",
      "crisp, forward",
      "MUSES02-like, thinner lines",
      "least op-amp-sounding",
      "tube-like",
      "softened extreme treble",
      "warm (vs LT1364)"
    ],
    "typical_uses": [
      "Drop-in upgrade for NJM4580/NE5532 sockets in DACs and preamps",
      "Op-amp rolling in socketed headphone amps and DACs",
      "DIY preamp, line and LPF stages",
      "OEM: TEAC AP-507, Ibanez BT Mini, VentureCraft VALOQ"
    ],
    "caveats": [
      "Praise is subjective: no ASR or Samuel Groner bench data, and Head-Fi round-up figures not captured.",
      "The 'least opamp-sounding / almost OPA627' quotes may come from the Opamp thread, not the Burson round-up.",
      "Bipolar input: 100 nA typ / 500 nA max bias, far above FET parts; mind high source impedances.",
      "Output drive and stability not yet checked; read the datasheet before driving headphones directly.",
      "One Head-Fi poster heard no difference from MUSES02 in an LPF position."
    ],
